Z||000013||terryk||07-03-2000||08:23 PM||||Then I refer you back to my first post. It's one thing for me to dig a hole for myself but quite another to dig a hole for *you*. I'm always worried someone will start a swap and realize it might be over their head. Now it's my problem 'cause I got them into it.<P>It seems to work better if you decide on the swap and get started then ask questions as to how to resolve the particulars. If you choose a swap that has already been done, then you know the hole's not too deep.<P>Of all the swaps, the most detailed is the V8 Archie swap information.<P>Dave's site is pretty good to give you an idea although it's certainly not at the level of detail you want.<P>Terry<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||1
